    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a structured address form to owner creation while keeping the flat `address` backward-compatible.\n\n**Files touched (6):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties to the `OwnerFields` schema (so they appear in both the generated request DTO and the response DTO via `allOf`), and dropped `address` from the `required` list so the structured form validates. `city` stays required.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` persistent fields with plain accessors. The `@NotEmpty` on the composed `address` remains the backstop that enforces \"an address in either form must be present.\"\n\n3. **`rest/function/owner/StructuredAddress.java`** (new) \u2014 A small cohesive helper: normalizes whichever address fields are supplied (reusing `AddressNormalizer`), prefers structured over flat, and sets `address` to the composed value (`addressLine1`, plus a single space and `addressLine2` when present). Because everything downstream reads `owner.getAddress()`, they automatically see the structured value when present, falling back to flat.\n\n4. **`rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 Replaced the single flat-normalize line with one call to `StructuredAddress.apply(owner)`; the rest of the pipeline is untouched.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the two nullable columns at the end of the `owners` table (this is the dialect the tests use; `ddl-auto=none`).\n\n6. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 Appended two `NULL`s per seed row to match the new column count (the seed uses positional, column-less inserts).\n\n**Design choices for low structural impact:** the composition logic lives in a new single-method utility class (near-zero surrounding complexity) rather than growing `BuildOwner`; `OwnerMapper` needed no changes (MapStruct auto-maps the new fields by name); and the schema/data edits were placed at the end of the table to keep the churn to append-only. The update path (`ApplyOwner`) and other DB dialects were left alone since no endpoint/test exercises them.",
